one relevant   Office Notes  None relevant     Physical Examination  Laterality was established according to departmental  universal protocol  Examination of the left breast reveals a 2cm  mobile  firm   nodule subareolar     Assessment  Based on the clinical history and physical examination  an FNAB is  warranted     Procedure  The procedure and complications were explained to the patient and  verbal consent was obtained  Ultrasound was used for evaluation of the lesion  and guidance of the needle during the procedure in order to avoid the implant   Ultrasound showed a 1 7cm hypoechoic nodule  4 aspirates were performed using  23 and 25 gauge needles with anesthesia and without complications  2 slides were  stained for immediate evaluation  additional tissue was submitted for further  evaluation     Disposition  The immediate interpretation findings were not discussed with the  patient  The preliminary results were communicated to Dr  Hughes in person at 5  o clock P M      The signing pathologist attests that he she performed the procedure or  if  performed by a resident or fellow  directed and supervised the FNA procedure and  was immediately available to further assist the resident fellow before  during  and after the procedure  and has reviewed and confirmed the interpretation of  slides stained for immediate evaluation          Electronically Signed Out By  Amy Ly MD on REMOVED_DATE 15 33     Hormone Receptor Quantitation    QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS    Breast  left   cellblock  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    Rare tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein   The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein   The tumor cells show strong  3   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2   See note     Note   Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive  nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows     The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained     Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained     Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained     The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained     HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is  evaluated visually and reported as follows     Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or  incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells     Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete membrane  immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells     Show strong  3   overexpression  strong complete membrane  immunoreactivity in   30  of tumor cells     These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by  the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not  been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The  FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this  laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision            Electronically Signed Out By  Elena F  Brachtel MD on REMOVED_DATE 19 26      REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  FISH Quantitation Analyisis    FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION  FISH  FOR HER 2 NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION    BREAST  LEFT  CELLBLOCK  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     HER 2 neu gene in tumor cells  REMOVED_DATE  Amplified    See note     Note  Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER 2 signals  477  to  chromosome 17 signals  49  in 30 tumor cell nuclei  A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE  or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17  polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis     The results at or near the cutoff point  ranging from REMOVED_DATE   2 2  should be  interpreted with caution  Equivocal Amplification    Reference  Journal of Clinical Oncology 25 118 145   REMOVED_CASE_ID             Electronically Signed Out By  Elena F  Brachtel MD on REMOVED_DATE 17 46       CLINICAL HISTORY  46 year old female status