Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  03 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  03 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 15 44 CLINICAL DATA  Ductal carcinoma with positive margins outside biopsy for re excision and nodes  Patient is on implant radiotherapy protocol                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  RIGHT   SHAVE    EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  FIBROCYSTIC DISEASE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 2 OF 27 LYMPH NODES AND IN AXILLARY FAT  SEE NOTE  Note  In one lymph node  the metastatic focus spans less than 0 2cm  LYMPH NODE   RIGHT AXILLA   ADDITIONAL    THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The lymph node is present only on the intraoperative section  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 30                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Lymph Nodes  Right axilla   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  10 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 20 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are three specimens  Labeled  right breast biopsy re excision   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 7cm breast re excision specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm skin ellipse containing a 3 0cm well healed linear scar  There s an undesignated short suture on one aspect which is inked in black  with the opposite section inked in blue  There s undesignated long suture present on another aspect  There s a previously opened biopsy cavity measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  It is lined by a tan pink smooth shiny membrane  It is less than 0 1cm from the nearest margin and 0 4cm from skin ellipse  Biopsy cavity is surrounded by scattered focally tan yellow nodules measuring 0 3cm in greatest dimension  Section Code  A  deep margin  B E  biopsy cavity  F  biopsy cavity and uninvolved parenchyma  Labeled  right axillary contents   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of adipose tissue upon which multiple lymph nodes are extracted and submitted in cassettes G O  Labeled as  right breast shaved node   are two fragments of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm in aggregate  submitted entirely in cassettes O P  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm firm lymmph node frozen entirely as FX 1  now in Q  Resident  D