Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  01 REMOVED_MONTH 03 ACCESSIONED ON  01 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 09 57 CLINICAL DATA  52 year old female with grade 3 DCIS and invasive cancer  here for re excision                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA   HEALING BIOPSY SITE  RESIDUAL CARCINOMA IS NOT IDENTIFIED  BREAST  LEFT  SHAVED MARGIN LATERAL REMOVED_DATE OF CAVITY   EXCISION  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA   HEALING BIOPSY SITE  RESIDUAL CARCINOMA IS NOT IDENTIFIED  BREAST  LEFT  SHAVED MARGIN MEDIAL REMOVED_DATE OF CAVITY   EXCISION  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA  RESIDUAL CARCINOMA IS NOT IDENTIFIED  Diagnosis by  MELINDA J  FAN  MD Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 17 46                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast lumpectomy specimen short stitch superior  long stitch lateral  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm portion of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue with a short black stitch designating the superior and a long black stitch the lateral margin  The posterior margin is inked black  the anterior blue  the superior green and the inferior yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm hemorrhagic cavity which communicates with the anteroinferior margin and comes to 0 9cm of the medial  0 5cm of the posterior  0 9cm of the superior and 2 1cm of the lateral margins  Surrounding the cavity is dense gray white fibrous tissue with yellow orange areas consistent with fat necrosis  No discrete tumor is identified and representative sections are submitted from medial to lateral as A J  with the medial margin radially sectioned as A  and the lateral as J  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shaved margin medial half of cavity  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm portion of gray white to tan yellow fibroadipose tissue with no orientation  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a predominantly dense gray white fibrous cut surface with no discrete lesion or other gross abnormality  The specimen is entirely submitted as K N  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast final shaved margin lateral half of cavity  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm aggregate of gray white to tan yellow fibroadipose tissue fragments with no orientation  The fragments are serially sectioned to reveal predominantly dense gray white fibrous tissue with no discrete lesion or other gross abnormality  The specimen is entirely submitted as O P  Gross Description by  STEPHANIE KUEHN Resident  RANIA M  SELIEM  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION PART B  BREAST  LEFT  SHAVED MARGIN LATERAL REMOVED_DATE OF CAVITY  PART C  BREAST  LEFT  SHAVED MARGIN MEDIAL REMOVED_DATE OF CAVITY   , Excisional_biopsy_(Lumpectomy).
