Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  30 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  30 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 13 06 CLINICAL DATA  Rule out breast cancer                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  100    MODERATE TO POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  EXTENDING TO MULTIPLE INKED RESECTION MARGINS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor measures approximately 1 8cm in greatest dimension by gross examination  No definite vascular invasion is identified  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 13 35                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 07 34 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm portion of pink tan fibrofatty breast tissue  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal pink and white  shiny  semifirm cut surface  A representative section is frozen as frozen section  1  and saved frozen  The remaining tissue is submitted entirely in A through B  Resident  STAMATINA KAPTAIN  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST LEFT BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  EXTENDING TO THE MARGINS  O R  Resident  SCOTT D  URBAN  HMS O R  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST MASS   report_end  , not_surgery.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  03 AUG 98 ACCESSIONED ON  03 AUG 98 at 13 20 CLINICAL DATA  Re excision of left breast ductal carcinoma  invasive  Old biopsy cavity went to pectoralis  Also  mass in axilla                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION  RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  EXTENDING A SHORT DISTANCE FROM THE BIOPSY CAVITY  AND REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE DEEP MARGIN  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  Note  No residual invasive ductal carcinoma is seen  No angiolymphatic invasion is identified  BREAST  LEFT AXILLARY MASS   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  AT LEAST REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO THE INKED RESECTION MARGIN AT MULTIPLE FOCI  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  ONE LYMPH NODE  FREE OF METASTATIC CARCINOMA  Note  The axillary mass probably represents an invasive carcinoma arising in axillary breast tissue  The invasive lobular carcinoma surrounds  but does not invade  a single lymph node within the mass  No definitive angiolymphatic invasion is seen  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   MAPPING  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 2 OF 2 LYMPH NODES  Note  Keratin immunostains will be reported separately  Diagnosis by  Joseph Misdraji  MD Signed On  07 AUG 98 at 19 04 Staff Pathologist  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS  Left Axilla   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  10 AUG 98 at 13 40     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     Multiple immunohistochemical stains for keratin show no keratin positive tumor cells in the lymph nodes  Added by  Joseph Misdraji  MD Signed On  24 AUG 98 at 14 20 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  mass  left axilla plus left axillary sampling   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of fibroadipose tissue showing a central poorly circumscribed  white  hard branching area measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  The specimen surfaces are inked and representative sections are submitted in Cassettes A C  Also received in the same container is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm portion of adipose tissue  containing two lymph nodes  the largest measuring 1 5cm  Grossly  the lymph nodes are soft with fatty changes  The larger lymph node is submitted in Cassette D  the smaller in Cassette E  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  re excision  left breast   and with a note  old cavity went to pectoralis muscle   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm portion of breast tissue  The specimen is oriented by a long suture on its lateral margin and a short suture on its superior margin  Attached is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm ellipse of skin showing a 4 5cm central  healed  surgical scar  The specimen shows a REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm central cavity which is open on its superior aspect  The walls of the cavity are firm with focal  white firm areas  The inner surface is gray tan and focally granular  The wall is REMOVED_DATE from the closest superior margin and 0 8cm from the other margins  The specimen is inked and representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE  F G  Cavity wall with deep margin  H   Cavity wall with superior margin  I   Lateral margin  J   Medial margin  K L  Inferior margin  M   Cavity wall and overlying skin  Resident  SELIM NASSER  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION PART B  BREAST  LEFT AXILLARY MASS   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART C  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA    report_end  , 1st_Re-Excision.
