Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  01 REMOVED_MONTH 02 ACCESSIONED ON  01 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 14 49 CLINICAL DATA  Prior outside lumpectomy with sentinel node biopsy showed positive margins  Had chemo  Now for mastectomy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE CARCINOMA WITH LOBULAR AND DUCTAL FEATURES  MULTIPLE SMALL FOCI  AGGREGATING TO APPROXIMATELY REMOVED_DATE CM AND EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM OF THE DEEP MARGIN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  MICROSCOPIC FOCUS  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 15 33                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block A   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  10 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 13 31 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right simple mastectomy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm breast  product of a simple mastectomy  which is oriented with a short suture at the superior aspect and a long suture at the lateral aspect  A tan skin ellipse is present anteriorly which measures REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm and contains a REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm areola with nipple  A faint well healed linear scar measuring 1 8cm is present at the skin ellipse  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm ill defined  firm  stellate scar within the breast parenchyma subjacent to the medial end of the skin ellipse  The scar extends to the deep resection margin along a broad front  No residual tumor is grossly identified  The remaining breast parenchyma is composed predominantly of white tan fibrotic soft tissue  marbled with a small amount of yellow fatty tissue  Within the parenchyma  away from the scar  is a rubbery  well circumscribed solid and cystic mass measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm in greatest dimensions  This mass has a smooth tan white homogeneous cut surface in the solid areas  The cystic areas have a smooth lining and are filled with a straw colored clear fluid  This mass extends to within 0 2cm of the deep resection margin  The remaining breast parenchyma is remarkable only for focal fibrocystic change  The tissue is dissected and examined for lymph nodes but none are identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows  Section Code  A J  Scar to deep margin  scar is submitted entirely   K M  Representative sections of rubbery mas  N O  Uninvolved parenchyma  Resident  JOHN BRANDA  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  James Warren May Jr   M D  PART   BREAST RIGHT  SIMPLE MASTECTOMY , Mastectomy.
