s prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 12 34 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is an unoriented simple mastectomy specimen measuring 21 x 14 x 4 5cm  There is an overlying wrinkled  tan skin ellipse which has a 1 0cm retracted nipple  At one end of the skin ellipse  there is a 3 8cm well healed surgical incision  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm pink purple papule that approaches one skin margin  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm biopsy cavity which is fibrotic and hemorrhagic  The surrounding tissue shows fat necrosis  This biopsy cavity is located 1 5cm from the deep margin  No residual tumor is grossly appreciated  Further sectioning of the breast reveals yellow fatty tissue with a moderate amount of gray white fibrous tissue  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm firm  gray white nodule located 3 5cm from the skin margin  6 5cm from the biopsy cavity and grossly appears to approach the inked margin  No other lesions are grossly appreciated or palpated  SECTION CODE A  Biopsy cavity to deep margin  B E  Biopsy cavity  H  Additional firm gray white lesion  totally submitted  I  Skin with papule  J K  Random sections of remaining breast parenchyma  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is the product of a left modified radical mastectomy REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 7 0cm with an attached 17 x 10 x 3cm axillary tail  The overlying  wrinkled  tan skin ellipse measures REMOVED_DATE x 7 8cm  There is a 4 0cm well healed surgical incision in the inferolateral aspect located 0 5cm from the skin margin  The specimen is inked and serially sectioned to reveal REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm fibrotic and hemorrhagic biopsy cavity with surrounding fat necrosis  This biopsy cavity is located 1 0cm from the skin margin  0 8cm from the deep margin  and 0 5cm from the inferior margin  Sectioning through the remaining breast reveals predominantly yellow fatty tissue and a moderate amount of gray white fibrous tissue  There are two  firm  gray white nodules measuring REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm and  7 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  These two foci are located in the lateral aspect of the specimen 4 5cm from the superior skin margin  6 0cm to the cavity  No other lesions are grossly appreciated or palpated  Multiple lymph nodes are dissected from the axillary tail ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  The lymph nodes are focally cystic  Further sections are submitted as follows  L  Biopsy cavity to deep end  M N  Biopsy cavity to inferior margin  O  Biopsy cavity to skin  P Q  Nodules entirely submitted  R S  Random sections of remaining breast tissue  T V  Lymph nodes  W  From one lymph node  X  Representative sections of one lymph node  bisected  Y  Representative sections from one lymph node  bisected  Z AA  Representative sections of one lymph no