m  2 by John H Eichhorn M D   Electronically signed on Thursday REMOVED_MONTH  15   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 03 32 29PM  By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final  Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed  or corrected the diagnoses                 ADDENDUM NOTE   REASON   2 RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION  FISH   FOR HER 2 NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION    Breast  Right  12 00  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     HER 2 neu gene in tumor cells  REMOVED_DATE  Not Amplified    See note     Note  The average ratio of HER 2 signals to chromosome 17 signals varies from  1 5 to REMOVED_DATE depending on the area of tumor selected for FISH analysis  The  ratio is affected by the presence of only one chromosome 17 signal rather than  two signals in many tumor cells  This may reflect failure to detect two  chromosomes in many tumor cells rather than absence of second chromosome 17   As the tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 by immunohistochemistry   it is likely that there is no HER 2 gene amplification in the tumor cells in  this biopsy  However  FISH analysis should be repeated when the tumor is  excised   Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER 2 signals  398  to chromosome  17 signals  237  in 180 tumor cell nuclei  A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or  equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17  polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis   The results at or near the cutoff point  ranging from REMOVED_DATE   2 2  should be  interpreted with caution  Equivocal Amplification   Reference  Journal of  Clinical Oncology 25 118 145   REMOVED_CASE_ID          Addendum  3 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on Wednesday REMOVED_MONTH 21    REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 02 52 06PM  By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final  Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed  or corre