Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  22 MAY 00 ACCESSIONED ON  22 MAY 00 at 10 48 CLINICAL DATA  Patient has breast cancer and is undergoing chemotherapy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION  RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU GRADE 1   SEE TABLE  1  FOCAL ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU Tumor size  Scattered small foci involving 4 of 7 blocks  Grade  1 Margin of ductal carcinoma in situ  Ductal carcinoma in situ focally extends to less than 0 2cm from the inked margin of the specimen  Diagnosis by  Ben Zion Pilch  M D  Signed On  25 MAY 00 at 19 10                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only is a 6 x 5 x 2cm portion of breast with a overlying REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm tan ellipse of skin  The skin has a central 3 5cm well healed linear scar with a 0 2cm red papule at the end of the scar  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 5 x 2 x 1cm area of thin fibrous tissue and focal hemorrhage consistent with a previous biopsy cavity  This area abuts multiple  3  soft tissue margins  On the outskirts of this area is a 0 5cm tan pink firm nodule coming to within 0 2cm from the nearest margin  The remaining breast tissue is dense  lobular fibrofatty breast tissue with a few blue dome based cysts  This fibrous tissue surrounds and is contiguous through the biopsy area  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A  Nodule B F  Representative G  Skin lesion Gross Description by  SHANNON SCHUTZ Resident  MANCONG ZHANG  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   BRAEST  LEFT   RE EXCISION   report_end  , Excisional_biopsy_(Lumpectomy).
