ue which is bisected and submitted in L  Labeled  lymph node    REMOVED_CASE_ID   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm portion of tan white soft tissue which is bisected and submitted in M  Labeled  lymph node    REMOVED_CASE_ID   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm portion of tan white soft tissue which is bisected and submitted in N  Labeled  right axillary contents  level I  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 3cm portion of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue containing four lymph nodes  all less than 0 5cm in maximum dimension  Three nodes are submitted in O A  one node in O B  Labeled  right axillary contents  level II  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm aggregate of multiple small fragments of friable tan yellow fibroadipose tissue containing one REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm lymph node which is bisected and submitted in P  Labeled  Q  right axillary nodes  level 1 B  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm aggregate of multiple small  friable fragments of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue containing a single REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm elongated portion of fibrous tissue submitted in Q  Labeled  right breast re excision  is a 20 gm  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 9cm right breast excision specimen which is partially covered by a REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm skin ellipse  the specimen is unoriented  The skin ellipse includes a central 2 2cm in length  well healed scar  The outer resection margins consist of lobular tan yellow fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is inked in black  with yellow overlay indicating the deep margin and green overlay indicating a resection margin parallel to the long axis of the specimen  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm stellate area of firm  tan brown to red discoloration extending to one resection margin parallel to the long axis  to within 0 5cm of the other margin parallel to the long axis  0 5cm from one margin perpendicular to the long axis  0 5cm from the other 