Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  05 REMOVED_MONTH 01 ACCESSIONED ON  05 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 15 47 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast re excision for carcinoma due to close margin                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  MELINDA J  FAN  MD Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 21 14                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast re excision  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm dome shaped tissue which is oriented by the surgeon with a short stitch designating anterior true margin of the specimen  measuring approximately REMOVED_DATE to 0 8cm    and a long stitch designating superior aspect of the specimen  The remainder of the specimen consists of exposed biopsy cavity  The designated true margins of the specimen are entirely inked black  The specimen are submitted as follows  A E  anterior margin  from lateral to medial F M  the superior margin  from lateral to medial Also received in the same container are two fragments of skin and fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassette N  Resident  LAN WANG  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION , Excisional_biopsy_(Lumpectomy).
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  10 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  10 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 08 54 CLINICAL DATA  History of lobular carcinoma with negative lymph nodes                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA AND LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEE NOTE  2  ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA  NOTE  The infiltrating carcinoma focally abuts an inked resection margin  the in situ component extends to within 1 0mm of an inked margin  No definite lymphatic or vascular invasion is identified  Tumor is present throughout the entire specimen  measuring 4 0cm on gross examination  Receptor studies will be done on the formalin fixed tissue  Diagnosis by  Kathleen K  Hansen  MD Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 09                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 09 07 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm fragment of fibrofatty breast tissue with a central firmness to palpation  Specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 0 3cm firm white area within less than 0 3cm of an inked surface  The remainder of the tissue is unremarkable  The lesion is submitted in cassettes A and B  the remainder of the tissue is in C through G  Resident  Jacqueline Haas  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     Gross Dx  RIGHT BREAST MASS   EXCISION  SMALL LESION TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  Douglas B  Flieder  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Asif Rashid  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Excisional_biopsy_(Lumpectomy).
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  27 REMOVED_MONTH 00 ACCESSIONED ON  27 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 11 27 CLINICAL DATA  85 y o  female with left breast mass  R O carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   NEEDLE CORE BIOPSIES  B CELL LYMPHOMA CONSISTENT WITH EXTRANODAL MARGINAL ZONE B CELL LYMPHOMA OF MUCOSA ASSOCIATED LYMPHOID TISSUE  MALT  TYPE  NOTE  There is a dense lymphoid infiltrate with focal reactive gemmal centers and a diffuse infiltrate of monomorphous small round lymphocytes  Focally  there are medium sized  irregular cells consistent with marginal zone cells  The differential diagnosis includes small lymphocytic lymphoma  follicle center lymphoma  mantle cell lymphoma and MALT type lymphoma  Immunoperoxidase stains show a  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   phenotype consistent with MALT type lymphoma  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 10 39                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOPEROXIDASE STAINS  PARAFFIN SECTIONS  With antibodies to immunoglobulin heavy and light chains there is high background  With antibody to B lineage antigen  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  there is staining of most cells in a diffuse pattern  The B cells are negative for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   With antibody to T lineage associated antigens   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   there is staining of many small cells scattered within the tissue  A  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  stain shows large irregular follicular dendritic cell meshworks  Similar staining is seen with  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   With antibody to bcl 2 tumor cells are positive and germinal centers are negative  The cells are negative for cyclin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Together with the morphologic features on routine sections  these results support the diagnosis of extranodal marginal zone B cell lymphoma and tend to exclude mantle cell  follicular and small lymphocytic lymphoma  See note  NOTE  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 10 39 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  with no designation as to site  are 9 cores of yellow pink fibroadipose tissue ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm which are submitted in toto to cassette A  Gross Description by  Robert F Donnell Resident  KRISTINA M  BRAATEN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  Gerald Joseph Doyle  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY , not_surgery.
