ecimen is black inked and serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm ill defined  firm  gritty  and tan white mass which extends into the dermis and involves the nipple  An ill define lesion is 0 4cm from the superior margin 0 7cm from the inferior margin  2 5cm from the medial margin  and 3 1cm from the lateral margin and 3 2cm from the posterior margin  In addition to the tumor associated with nipple  there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm tan white  stellate  firm  and ill defined lesion present in the superior lateral portion of the specimen  abutting the superior margin and lateral margin  1 0cm from the posterior margin  2 2cm from the inferior margin  and 2 1cm from the skin surface  Representative sections are submitted as per section code  K M  tumor with superior margin N O  tumor and nipple with inferior margin P  tumor and nipple and skin lesion  Q R  surrounding skin with underlying fibrofatty parenchyma S  second lesion with superior margin T  second lesion with superior lateral margin U  second lesion with abutting superior and posterior   overinked yellow  margin V  uninvolved breast parenchyma Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left final shaved superior half cavity  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm fragment of cauterized and slightly firm yellow fibrofatty tissue which is serially sectioned and entirely submitted into cassette W BB  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left final shave inferior half cavity  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm fragment of unoriented yellow fibrofatty and cauterized soft tissue which is serially sectioned and entirely submitted into cassette CC II  Resident  PAUL MICHAELS  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Sarah P Thayer  M D