SCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary sentinel node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm tan red rubbery fatty lymph node  for which the fat is removed and the lymph node is frozen entirely as FX 1 and 2  now as A and B respectively  The remaining fat is entirely submitted as C  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast re excision   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm portion of fibrofatty breast tissue which has a REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm tan irregular skin ellipse along the anterior aspect  There is a short stitch designating superior and long stitch designating lateral  the medial aspect is black inked  the lateral aspect is blue inked  Specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm hemorrhagic cavity surrounded by fat necrosis which communicates with the anterior and posterior aspect  The cavity comes to within 0 3cm of the superior  medial  lateral  superior  and inferior margins  No discrete nodules are grossly identified  The remaining parenchyma is predominantly yellow lobulated fatty tissue  Representative sections are submitted sequentially from posterior to anterior as follows  D  cavity through superior medial margin  E F  cavity to medial inferior margin  G  cavity to lateral margin  H  cavity to medial margin  I  cavity to superior margin  J  cavity to superior margin  K  cavity to medial margin  I  cavity to superior margin  J  cavity to inferior margin  K  cavity to medial margin  L  cavity to lateral margin  M  cavity to anterior margin  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary contents   is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm aggregate of fibrofatty tissue  which contains multiple tan red rubbery lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 1 8cm in greatest dimension  Representative sections are submitted as follows  N  four suspected whole lymph nodes  O  three suspected whole lymph nodes  P Q  two suspected whole lymph nodes in each  R  entire trisected largest lymph node  Gross Description by  LORI MARINI Resident  SOHEIL DADRAS  MD  PHD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LYMPH NODE  SENTINEL LEFT AXILLARY  METASTATIC ADENOCARCINOMA  O R  Resident  SHABIN NANJI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Ben Zion Pilch  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  Wendy Y Chen  M D  PART A  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL   EXCISION PART B  BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION PART C  AXILLARY CONTENTS  LEFT   EXCISION , Excisional_biopsy_(Lumpectomy).
